(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["KPZ, one loop, dimensionful", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"768da233-9bda-4b0e-85b8-8e22d72b8d12"],

Cell["\<\
The KPZ equation dt h = nu lap h + lambda/2 (grad h)^2 + noise, with noise \
variance 2 D, written as an MSR action. The ansatz has the form of the bare \
action. The Galilean symmetry protects the coefficient 1 of dt h (Ward \
identity) and the non-linearity lambda (not checkable in v1: that needs d_s \
Gamma3, so it is declared NonRenormalised).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"69929feb-c3f7-4382-bbe4-b8909c6fd74c"],

Cell["Get[\"~/Physics/Sources/FRGscalarMSR/FRGscalarMSR.wl\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e2a573df-3491-4f39-9b38-c7892a58a907"],

Cell["\<\
theory = DefineTheory[\"Scalars\" -> {h}, \"Dimension\" -> Dim];
ansatz = DefineAnsatz[theory, \"Density\" -> hbar (dt[h] - nuk lap[h] - \
lamk/2 grad[h].grad[h]) - Dk hbar^2,
  \"Couplings\" -> {nuk, lamk, Dk}];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"93b0786a-160a-4711-9fb1-dae891b0b0db"],

Cell["\<\
symmetries = DeclareSymmetries[ansatz,
  Protected[{hbar, h}, \"Frequency\" -> 1, \"Momentum\" -> 0, \"Reason\" -> \
\"Galilean Ward identity\"],
  Protected[{h, hbar}, \"Frequency\" -> 0, \"Momentum\" -> 0, \"Reason\" -> \
\"h -> h + c (shift symmetry)\"],
  Neglected[_, \"Reason\" -> \"beyond the ansatz\"], NonRenormalised[lamk, \
\"Reason\" -> \"Galilean invariance\"],
  \"TruncationOrders\" -> <|\"Frequency\" -> 2, \"Momentum\" -> 1|>];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"fbba357a-b902-404c-99ca-4bc8a87ffd23"],

Cell["\<\
vertices = BuildVertices[ansatz];
regulator = DefineRegulator[ansatz, {hbar, h} -> nuk q^2 rn[q^2/k^2], {hbar, \
hbar} -> -2 Dk rd[q^2/k^2], \"Shapes\" -> {rn, rd}];
prop = BuildPropagator[vertices, regulator];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c36b940e-ef14-4fa5-85af-ee3efb889c74"],

Cell["\<\
flows = CheckClosure[IntegrateFrequencies[ProjectOnMonomials[\
BuildLoopIntegrands[vertices, prop, regulator], symmetries]], symmetries];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"441abab1-6b0a-4342-98a5-0dc896b11e2b"],

Cell["\<\
equations = AssembleEquations[flows];
ShowEquation[equations, nuk]
ShowEquation[equations, Dk]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a6f96d33-1a4f-4cb4-bb69-078851903ea9"],

Cell["oracle = RunOracle[equations, \"ZeroFlows\" -> True];", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d408ba1f-fcda-4ab7-956e-983e390657df"],

Cell["Check of the loop normalisation against Canet's flow", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a5a59f86-3f70-4862-8fbc-223ad2641f33"],

Cell["\<\
L. Canet, arXiv:2509.01472, Eq. (20): with the Litim cutoff r(y) = (1/y - 1) \
theta(1 - y) in both sectors, the dimensionless coupling g = v_d k^(d-2) \
lambda^2 D/nu^3 flows as d_s g = g (d - 2 - eta_D + 3 eta_nu), with d_s nu = \
-eta_nu nu, d_s D = -eta_D D. We integrate our two equations over q with the \
Litim shape (Int d^dq/(2 Pi)^d f = v_d k^d/2 Int_0^1 y^(d/2-1) f dy), solve \
the linear system for eta_nu and eta_D, and compare. The difference is \
exactly 0 for every d: this checks the prefactor, sign and 2 Pi of the loop \
formula (not the Gamma4 tadpole, absent here).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"35ddd4f0-74f5-4f4b-9157-e5655ba2d7df"],

Cell["\<\
litim = {rn -> Function[y, 1/y - 1], rd -> Function[y, 1/y - 1]};
litimIntegral[f_] := Module[{g = Expand[Together[f /. q -> k Sqrt[y] /. \
litim] y^(d/2 - 1)], terms},
  terms = If[Head[g] === Plus, List @@ g, {g}];
  vd k^d/2 Total[(# /. y -> 1)/(Exponent[#, y] + 1) & /@ terms]];
flowOf[c_] := litimIntegral[EquationOf[equations, c][\"Integrand\"] /. Dim -> \
d];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"23be36c8-b47a-4f73-9b32-795c566e172b"],

Cell["\<\
etas = First[Solve[{-etanu nuk == (flowOf[nuk] /. {dsCoupling[nuk] -> -etanu \
nuk, dsCoupling[Dk] -> -etaD Dk}),
     -etaD Dk == (flowOf[Dk] /. {dsCoupling[nuk] -> -etanu nuk, \
dsCoupling[Dk] -> -etaD Dk})}, {etanu, etaD}]];
bracket = Together[(d - 2 - etaD + 3 etanu) /. etas /. lamk -> Sqrt[g \
nuk^3/(vd k^(d - 2) Dk)]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a9eee056-1f8d-4c07-b78b-d92c4475aaaa"],

Cell["\<\
canet = (2 d^6 + 4 d^5 - d^4 (7 g + 8) - 2 d^3 (3 g + 8) + d^2 g (3 g + 20) - \
d (g - 8) g - 2 g^2)/
   (2 d^5 + 8 d^4 + d^3 (8 - 3 g) - 2 d^2 g + d g (g + 8) - g^2);
Together[bracket - canet]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b3de8901-bc6a-4479-9f3f-98183d971fd1"],

Cell["Dimensionless flow and the FlowRG file", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"88055464-39d1-48fb-ba72-456f0b58dac5"],

Cell["\<\
The same, done by the library: dimensions from the ansatz in the basis (k, \
nuk, Dk), the dimensionless flow of lamk (linear part only: lambda is \
NonRenormalised) and the eta system, then the FlowRG file for d = 2. \
tests/acceptance/KPZAdimensional.wl checks that this output gives Canet's Eq. \
(20) exactly.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"de7d2b0f-d6b5-4c5e-8afa-e182890d4e2e"],

Cell["\<\
dims = DeriveDimensions[ansatz, \"References\" -> {nuk -> \"nu\", Dk -> \
\"D\"}];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d0ebb5a8-265a-4230-9cea-87dd59e0f303"],

Cell["\<\
adim = AdimensionalEquations[equations, dims];
ShowBeta[adim, lamk]
ShowEtaSystem[adim]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"90fc62ba-0d4f-4e53-ab97-e2ebaf17c67f"],

Cell["\<\
ExportJulia[adim, \"Dimension\" -> 2, \"File\" -> \
FileNameJoin[{$TemporaryDirectory, \"KPZ\", \"Equations2D.jl\"}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9f3a53b2-7a90-416a-b1cc-62641fba4d69"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"14.3 for Linux x86 (64-bit) (July 8, 2025)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"bac4b446-e164-413d-b92c-2fae239d37fa"
]
